/-
  `O`-version of the §12-type totally separated design, q = 19, rational twist `t = 71/8` (all three embeddings
  equal `t`), the 27 rows of degrees 4..12.  `O = Z[θ]`, θ³ + θ² − 6θ − 7 = 0.

  Namespace `DesignT71over8Cert`: an `S₃`-symmetric test polynomial `q ∈ T_{71/8}` with `q(0) = 0` (orbit
  coefficients over m0, m100, m110, m111, m200, m210, m211, m220, m221, m222; c200 < 0, c211 > 0, c210, c221 < 0).
    * `q_mem`, `p0_mem`: `q, p0 ∈ T_t` (explicit `Σ_j g(u_j)·h_j`, `g(x) = (x − t)² + 19`), `q_zero`, `p0_zero`.
    * `dq_neg_shift` (outside the box, radius R = 80): after `a₁ = d + 80`, `−Δq` is an explicit sum of
      `c·M·(Σ vᵢ zᵢ)²` (c > 0, M a monomial, zᵢ ∈ {1, d, a₂, a₃, b₁, b₂, b₃} or two-term midpoint squares) plus a
      polynomial with nonnegative coefficients (`ring` + `positivity`).  The two-term squares alone do not suffice
      for this `q`; the squares with three or four terms use positive cross terms such as `a₃b₂b₃`.
      `dq_neg_of_some_coord_ge` (six coordinates > 0, one of them ≥ 80): `Δq < 0`.  No norm condition is used.
    * `no_design_of_box_table` (ASSUMPTION `hbox`: every piece with all six coordinates ≤ 80 has `Δq < 0`; positive
      coordinates, nonnegative weights, the design equations for `q` and `p0`): `False`.
      The table `hbox` was checked exactly outside Lean for the totally positive elements of `O` with all
      embeddings ≤ 80 (B_80: 26,948 elements; 121,752,610 pairs up to the simultaneous Galois action and all
      363,110,826 unordered pairs), integer arithmetic on characteristic polynomials (`__int128`).  Lean does not see `O`.
  The dictionary "design ⟺ `Σ n Δp = p(0)` for all `p ∈ T_t`" (earlier notes, on paper) is not formalised here.
-/
import Mathlib

set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

namespace DesignT71over8Cert

/-- `g(x) = (x − t)² + 19` (`t = 71/8`); the eight points `(t ± i√19)³` are the common zeros of `g(u₁), g(u₂), g(u₃)`. -/
noncomputable def g (x : ℝ) : ℝ := x^2 - (71/4)*x + (6257/64)

